# The Razor Standard — all-inclusive engineering playbook

This file is auto-loaded by GitHub Copilot Chat for every request in this
workspace (`.github/copilot-instructions.md`). It is the single source of
truth for two related standards: how code should be written (Part I), and
how existing dead code gets found, visualized, and safely removed
(Part II). Named for Occam's razor — don't multiply abstractions, and
don't let unreferenced code linger, beyond necessity.

> **The best code is the code you never wrote — and the second-best code
> is the code that's already been deleted.**

One companion file supports Part II: [`scripts/dead_code_graph.py`](./scripts/dead_code_graph.py),
a renderer for the graphical reports in section 15, with a sample input/
output alongside it. Every rule and protocol otherwise lives in this one
document.

